# n2i-dev-cycle skill config.
# Copy to  <target repo root>/.n2i-dev-cycle/config  (next to the .git / .slnx).
# The skill reads this file if present; Phase 1 offers to create it on the first run.
# The whole .n2i-dev-cycle/ folder is per-developer local state — add one line to the
# target repo's .gitignore:
#   .n2i-dev-cycle/
# The folder may also hold an optional hand-written notes.md (personal repo gotchas)
# and the skill-generated progress.md checkpoint ledger.
# All keys optional — skill falls back to defaults when unset. Format: KEY=value, one per line.

# Branch name prefix for new feature branches (e.g. "mb/" -> mb/17-add-foo).
# Default: derived from git user initials, else "dev/".
BRANCH_PREFIX=mb/

# Default scope when BOTH backend and frontend are detected and no scope token given.
# One of: backend | frontend | both. Default: ask (skill prompts when unset).
# DEFAULT_SCOPE=both

# Force forge instead of auto-detecting from git remote. Optional.
# One of: gitlab | github. Default: auto-detect from remote URL.
# FORGE=gitlab

# Database engine for new migration scripts. One of: postgres | sqlserver | auto.
# Default: postgres. Set sqlserver only for legacy apps not yet migrated to PG.
# 'auto' detects from the migrator call / csproj packages, falling back to postgres.
# Ignore entirely if the project doesn't use DbUp — see MIGRATION_STANDARDS.
# DB_ENGINE=postgres

# Migration-mode status doc filename (searched within the repo). Optional.
# Enables Migration input mode + status-table updates. Default: migration mode off.
# MIGRATION_DOC=migration-status.md

# --- Stack adaptation (set these to run the skill on any tech stack) ---------
# When unset, the skill auto-detects a .NET solution + an Angular/Node frontend
# and uses `dotnet` / `npm` commands. Set the keys below for any other stack.

# Validation command(s) per side — a shell snippet run in Phase 5, looped until it
# exits 0. Include format + build + unit tests for that side. Runs from the repo root
# ($SLN / $FRONTEND are available). Only the in-scope side's snippet runs.
# BACKEND_VALIDATE_CMD=cargo fmt --check && cargo build && cargo test
# FRONTEND_VALIDATE_CMD=cd "$FRONTEND" && pnpm lint && pnpm build && pnpm test

# End-to-end command — run in Phase 6 against the affected specs. Optional.
# E2E_CMD=npx playwright test

# Repo-owned standards files — a path (relative to repo root) to the project's own
# backend / frontend / migration conventions, when the repo keeps its own instead of
# using the skill's references/*.md defaults. Common choice: backend/CLAUDE.md etc.
# Phase 3 reads the pointed-at file as authoritative and skips the matching skill
# reference. The working dir's own CLAUDE.md still auto-loads and wins on conflict.
# BACKEND_STANDARDS=src/Api/CLAUDE.md
# FRONTEND_STANDARDS=web/CLAUDE.md
# MIGRATION_STANDARDS=db/migrations/README.md
